messages:
elaine: Heads up, PR #482 in docs updates the /evaluate webhook callback payload. There's confusion in the examples where `status` is shown as 200 in one example and `"success"` in another. Can someone review? First post has code blocks.

matt: looking... can you paste the two snippets?

elaine: Sure — current docs have:

```json
{
  "request_id": "req_123",
  "status": 200,
  "result": { "score": 0.93 }
}
```

and elsewhere:

```json
{
  "request_id": "req_123",
  "status": "success",
  "result": [ { "score": 0.93 } ]
}
```

matt: ok thats bad. server actually sends `status: "succeeded"` and `result` is an object (not an array). we should standardize to string status and object result. also we use `score` as float between 0-1. add schema and example.

jordan: i'll update the PR with a single canonical example and add an explicit JSON Schema snippet. also add migration note for clients expecting numeric status codes.

samir: don't forget SDK snippet for node — a lot of users copy that. small fetch example please.

elaine: posted a quick node snippet — can someone sanity check? 

```js
// node fetch example for webhook handler
app.post('/callbacks', express.json(), (req, res) => {
  const body = req.body;
  if (body.status !== 'succeeded') {
    // retry logic
  }
  console.log(body.result.score);
  res.sendStatus(200);
});
```

devx-bot: Added a lint warning in PR: docs/examples should match runtime schema. :robot_face:

alyssa: small nit: use `result.score` or `result[]`? which one did runtime emit?

matt: runtime emits object. so `result.score`.

jordan: merging change to canonical example + node snippet + migration note. will also add a short Python async snippet.

elaine: awesome, thanks. link to PR: https://github.com/redwood-inference/docs/pull/482 :thumbsup:

samir: follow-up: can we add a short test that validates example JSON against the schema? reduces regressions.

jordan: yep adding simple jest test to docs repo.

matt: :eyes: will review the test. once green i'll merge.
